A parent requires their child to complete all homework immediately after school, before any leisure activities, and does not allow discussion about the schedule. The child has asked to sometimes do homework after dinner or take short breaks first, saying it would help them focus better. The parent is considering whether to adjust the rule.

If you were advising this parent, what would you recommend?:
"A" = Discuss daily workload with the child and adjust timing when they show consistent responsibility.
"B" = Allow a 10-minute break after school, but homework must still come before dinner and screen time.
"C" = Let the child manage their own homework schedule, with parents checking only that it’s completed.
"D" = Let the child choose between “right after school” or “right after dinner,” with no other options.
"E" = Keep the current rule unchanged—children should follow the homework schedule set by parents without debate.

